Release v0.4.0

The scrolling release. The transcript moves from a reversed list to an ordinary
top-anchored one, because a reversed list anchors on the row at the bottom of the
viewport and therefore grows a row *upward* by exactly the height it gains — measured,
192px for a 48px row grown to 200px, against zero in an ordinary list. That one
property was behind "it opens upwards", "it closes the rows I'm reading" and most of
"it jumps about", and the six mechanisms stacked on top of it were patches over it.

Everything that moves a list now either is the reader's gesture or says so before it
moves. Frame times over 24,053 frames with the reader scrolling: 11.7% of frames over
the 11ms budget before, 5.4% after, and 1.4% over 33ms.

`docs/releases/v0.4.0.md` carries the full account, including a section on what is not
verified.

versionCode 4 -> 5, versionName 0.3.0 -> 0.4.0, and the release APK built locally
reports 5 / 0.4.0 rather than merely being tagged as such.